    "industrial_process_notes": "Patented in 1948; introduced to commercial markets by Borg-Warner Corporation in 1954. Made by grafting/blending a SAN-forming mixture of styrene and acrylonitrile with polybutadiene rubber particles, giving a rubber-toughened matrix. Monomers derive from petroleum and natural gas feedstocks; production uses roughly 95.34 MJ/kg of resin.",
